This ordinary program reads a supplied name. It shows the idea of using context; it is not an AI model.

```javascript
function greet(context) {
  return "Hello, " + context.name + "!";
}
const context = { name: "Neri" };
console.log(greet(context));
```

It prints Hello, Neri!. The input supplies Neri; the function did not need to learn a new rule.
